# Android 17 PBRP recovery sources

Based on the LineageOS 24 / Android 17 manifest. The upstream structure is
preserved: `default.xml`, `snippets/lineage.xml` and the kernel snippets.
`default.xml` also includes `recovery.xml` for our recovery forks, device tree,
kernel, required tools and project replacements. `vendor/utils` owns the
`pb_build.sh` link into `vendor/pb`.

Shared defaults track LineageOS 24, the official Android 17 release tag and
`pbrp-a17` for our forks. Vendor exceptions retain their upstream branches.
There are no separate Alioth aliases or commit-pin snapshots. Record exact
build revisions with `repo manifest -r -o /path/to/build-manifest.xml` when
producing a release.

## Build

```bash
mkdir -p ~/pbrp-alioth-a17
cd ~/pbrp-alioth-a17
repo init -u https://github.com/pbrp-alioth-a17/manifest -b pbrp-a17
repo sync -c -j8
source build/envsetup.sh
lunch pb_alioth cp2a user
recoverybuild bootimage -j4
```

Select the product, release, variant and image target required by another port.
See the [shared recovery commands](https://github.com/pbrp-alioth-a17/android_bootable_recovery/blob/pbrp-a17/README.md)
and [Alioth build and packaging instructions](https://github.com/pbrp-alioth-a17/device_xiaomi_alioth-pbrp/blob/pbrp-a17/README.md).
Alioth's complete kernel/staging wrapper remains available at
`device/xiaomi/alioth/tools/build-recovery.sh`. Use matching ROM metadata for
packaging. Do not flash Alioth's placeholder vendor_boot image.

## Validation

The manifest was checked with repo's actual parser against the approved
1,223-project recovery checkout: project URLs, branch/tag selection and
copy/link operations are preserved. The recovery-specific exclusions retain
that checkout scope without rewriting the upstream project lists.

Android dependencies were audited over the network on 2026-10-12. Build and
Boot/installer packaging checks passed; detailed runtime evidence and limits
are in the device README. Latest UI, portability and dependency changes still
require their exact image's phone checks. No device access or flashing was used
for this manifest reorganization.
